# The edge: the browser's ONE origin. It signs the person in from the
# authority's fixture, routes /v1/codefly-base to this solution's backend with that
# person's Work Context, and serves the solution's page on every other path.
#
# Opening the page at the shell's own port instead is the mistake this file
# exists to prevent: the shell asks the edge for /auth/session on its own
# origin, finds nothing, and says so.
# ADDED TO THE SCAFFOLD: the store's own page calls are routed too (through the
# hop), so the scenarios can call every procedure the store's catalog declares
# on a person's own session. The solution's page calls nothing this way.
MODULES=codefly-base,documents
DOCUMENTS_CONNECT=${endpoint:authority/hop/http}
DOCUMENTS_RPC=documents.v1.DocumentsService
CODEFLY_BASE_REST=${endpoint:codefly-base/backend/http}
FRONTEND=${endpoint:codefly-base/web/http}
